<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xs:schema xmlns:tns="http://schema.webpdf.de/1.0/operation" elementFormDefault="qualified"
           targetNamespace="http://schema.webpdf.de/1.0/operation" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <xs:include schemaLocation="operation-common.xsd"/>
    <xs:complexType name="PdfaType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>When using the "Pdfa" web service, the <code>&lt;convert&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;analyze&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;invoice&gt;</code> operations can be used.
                </p>
                <p>The <code>convert</code> operation is used to convert PDF documents to PDF/A, while the <code>analyze</code> operation is used to validate existing PDF/A documents.
                    The <code>invoice</code> operation validates an electronic invoice (ZUGFeRD, Factur-X, XRechnung) that is supplied as a plain XML document, without a PDF carrying it.
                </p>
                <p>The three operations cover the e-invoicing subject of this web service together: <code>convert &gt; zugferd</code> embeds an invoice, <code>analyze</code> checks an invoice that is already embedded, and <code>invoice</code> checks an invoice without a PDF carrier.
                    The invoice validation is therefore available whenever the "Pdfa" web service is available.
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:choice>
            <xs:element id="pdfaConvertId" name="convert">
                <xs:annotation>
                    <xs:documentation>
                        <p>Used to convert a PDF document to PDF/A.</p>
                    </xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                    <xs:all>
                        <xs:element name="zugferd" type="tns:ZugferdType" minOccurs="0"/>
                        <xs:element name="errorCorrection" type="tns:PdfaErrorCorrectionType" minOccurs="0"
                        />
                    </xs:all>
                    <xs:attribute name="level" default="3b" type="tns:PdfaLevelType">
                        <xs:annotation>
                            <xs:documentation>
                                <p>Specifies the compliance level when creating or validating PDF/A documents (as specified in ISO 19005).</p>
                            </xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:attribute>
                    <xs:attribute name="imageQuality" default="75">
                        <xs:annotation>
                            <xs:documentation>
                                <p>The quality for images which must be transformed during the conversion because they use a compression which is not allowed (e.g. JPX is not allowed in PDF/A-1) is defined using this parameter. Values in a range from 1 to 100 are allowed whereby a higher value means better quality, but also larger PDF documents.</p>
                            </xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                        <xs:simpleType>
                            <xs:restriction base="xs:int">
                                <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
                                <xs:maxInclusive value="100"/>
                            </xs:restriction>
                        </xs:simpleType>
                    </xs:attribute>
                    <xs:attribute name="errorReport" default="none" type="tns:PdfaErrorReportType">
                        <xs:annotation>
                            <xs:documentation>
                                <p>This parameter is used to define whether and in which format the XML report for a failed conversion will be returned.
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>none = An XML report will not be returned</li>
                                        <li>message = The XML report will be returned as part of the error message</li>
                                        <li>file = The XML report will be saved in a file</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </p>
                            </xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:attribute>
                    <xs:attribute name="successReport" default="none" type="tns:PdfaSuccessReportType">
                        <xs:annotation>
                            <xs:documentation>
                                <p>This parameter is used to define whether and in which format the XML report for a successful conversion will be returned.
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>none = An XML report will not be returned</li>
                                        <li>linked = The XML report will be appended at the end of the PDF/A document.</li>
                                        <li>zip = The PDF/A document and the XML report will be packaged together in a ZIP archive.</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <b>Tip:</b>
                                    The format of the document generated with "errorReport" and "successReport" is described by the http://schema.webpdf.de/1.0/report/pdfa.xsd schema.
                                </p>
                            </xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:attribute>
                    <xs:attribute name="autoTagging" default="false" type="xs:boolean">
                        <xs:annotation>
                            <xs:documentation>
                                <p>In order to convert a document to conformity levels PDF/A 1a-3a, the entire document must have appropriate structure information (tags). If auto tagging is enabled, the corresponding structure information (in the form of page tags) will be generated automatically before the actual conversion.</p>
                            </xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:attribute>
                </xs:complexType>
            </xs:element>
            <xs:element id="pdfaAnalyzeId" name="analyze">
                <xs:annotation>
                    <xs:documentation>
                        <p>Used to validate an existing PDF/A document.</p>
                    </xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                    <xs:all>
                        <xs:element name="invoiceRuleValidation" type="tns:InvoiceRuleValidationType"
                                    minOccurs="0"/>
                    </xs:all>
                    <xs:attribute name="level" default="3b" type="tns:PdfaLevelType">
                        <xs:annotation>
                            <xs:documentation>
                                <p>Specifies the compliance level when creating or validating PDF/A documents (as specified in ISO 19005).</p>
                            </xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:attribute>
                </xs:complexType>
            </xs:element>
            <xs:element id="pdfaInvoiceId" name="invoice" type="tns:InvoiceType">
                <xs:annotation>
                    <xs:documentation>
                        <p>Used to validate an electronic invoice XML without a PDF carrier. The source
                            document of the request IS the invoice XML, and the response document is the
                            invoice validation report (root element "report" of "report/invoice.xsd").
                        </p>
                    </xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
            </xs:element>
        </xs:choice>
    </xs:complexType>
    <xs:simpleType name="PdfaLevelType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>Specifies the compliance level when creating or validating PDF/A documents (as specified in ISO 19005).</p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="1a"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="1b"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="2a"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="2b"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="2u"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="3a"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="3b"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="3u"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
    <xs:simpleType name="PdfaErrorReportType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>This parameter is used to define whether and in which format the XML report for a failed conversion will be returned.
                    <ul>
                        <li>none = An XML report will not be returned</li>
                        <li>message = The XML report will be returned as part of the error message</li>
                        <li>file = The XML report will be saved in a file</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="none"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="file"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="message"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
    <xs:simpleType name="PdfaSuccessReportType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>This parameter is used to define whether and in which format the XML report for a successful conversion will be returned.
                    <ul>
                        <li>none = An XML report will not be returned</li>
                        <li>linked = The XML report will be appended at the end of the PDF/A document.</li>
                        <li>zip = The PDF/A document and the XML report will be packaged together in a ZIP archive.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <b>Tip:</b>
                    The format of the document generated with "errorReport" and "successReport" is described by the http://schema.webpdf.de/1.0/report/pdfa.xsd schema.
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="none"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="zip"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="linked"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
    <xs:simpleType name="ZugferdVersionType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>Used to define the version of the ZUGFeRD XML file that should be embedded with "xmlFile".
                    Versions from 1.0 to 2.5 are supported.
                    Only the "Comfort" profile is available for version 1.0.
                    Meanwhile, the "Minimum", "Basic WL", "Basic", "EN16931" (Comfort), and "Extended" profiles are
                    supported for version 2.0.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <b>Note:</b>
                    Since version 2.x, the referenced profile "XRechnung" is additionally available. This profile has
                    been included specifically to include invoices for Germany, based on and under the sole
                    responsibility of KoSIT, Germany's central coordination agency for IT's e-invoice CIUS "XRechnung".
                    It is defined as the Standard for electronic invoices issued to public administrations, and
                    essentially adds specific business rules to EN 16931 in order to comply with national laws and
                    regulations.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <b>Note:</b>
                    Since version 2.1.1 ZUGFeRD and Factur-X are technically identical, and both formats use Factur-X as
                    common identification.
                </p>
                <p>
                    List of versions with the corresponding profiles:
                    <ul>
                        <li>v10Comfort</li>
                        <li>v20Minimum</li>
                        <li>v20BasicWL</li>
                        <li>v20Basic</li>
                        <li>v20EN16931</li>
                        <li>v20Extended</li>
                        <li>v21Minimum</li>
                        <li>v21BasicWL</li>
                        <li>v21Basic</li>
                        <li>v21EN16931</li>
                        <li>v21Extended</li>
                        <li>v21XRechnung</li>
                        <li>v22Minimum</li>
                        <li>v22BasicWL</li>
                        <li>v22Basic</li>
                        <li>v22EN16931</li>
                        <li>v22Extended</li>
                        <li>v22XRechnung</li>
                        <li>v23Minimum</li>
                        <li>v23BasicWL</li>
                        <li>v23Basic</li>
                        <li>v23EN16931</li>
                        <li>v23Extended</li>
                        <li>v23XRechnung</li>
                        <li>v24Minimum</li>
                        <li>v24BasicWL</li>
                        <li>v24Basic</li>
                        <li>v24EN16931</li>
                        <li>v24Extended</li>
                        <li>v24XRechnung</li>
                        <li>v25Minimum</li>
                        <li>v25BasicWL</li>
                        <li>v25Basic</li>
                        <li>v25EN16931</li>
                        <li>v25Extended</li>
                        <li>v25XRechnung</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="v10Comfort"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v20Minimum"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v20BasicWL"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v20Basic"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v20EN16931"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v20Extended"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v21Minimum"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v21BasicWL"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v21Basic"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v21EN16931"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v21Extended"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v21XRechnung"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v22Minimum"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v22BasicWL"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v22Basic"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v22EN16931"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v22Extended"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v22XRechnung"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v23Minimum"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v23BasicWL"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v23Basic"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v23EN16931"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v23Extended"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v23XRechnung"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v24Minimum"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v24BasicWL"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v24Basic"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v24EN16931"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v24Extended"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v24XRechnung"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v25Minimum"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v25BasicWL"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v25Basic"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v25EN16931"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v25Extended"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="v25XRechnung"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
    <xs:complexType name="ZugferdType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>This element can be optionally used to integrate a ZUGFeRD document. The document must at least be converted to PDF/A-3 format.</p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:all>
            <xs:element name="xmlFile" type="tns:ZugferdFileDataType"/>
            <xs:element name="invoiceRuleValidation" type="tns:InvoiceRuleValidationType" minOccurs="0"/>
        </xs:all>
    </xs:complexType>
    <xs:complexType name="ZugferdFileDataType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>ZUGFeRD file (XML) in "Base64 encoded" format. The ZUGFeRD XSD schema will be used to validate the file before embedding. If it is not valid, the operation will be aborted.</p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:simpleContent>
            <xs:extension base="xs:base64Binary">
                <xs:attributeGroup ref="tns:FileDataGroup"/>
                <xs:attribute name="version" default="v10Comfort" type="tns:ZugferdVersionType">
                    <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>
                            <p>Used to define the version of the ZUGFeRD XML file that should be embedded with "xmlFile".
                                Versions from 1.0 to 2.5 are supported.
                                Only the "Comfort" profile is available for version 1.0.
                                Meanwhile, the "Minimum", "Basic WL", "Basic", "EN16931"
                                (Comfort), and "Extended" profiles are supported for version 2.0.
                                Version 2.1.x contains the same profiles as version 2.0 and additionally defines the profile "X-Rechnung".
                                List of versions with the corresponding profiles:
                                <ul>
                                    <li>v10Comfort</li>
                                    <li>v20Minimum</li>
                                    <li>v20BasicWL</li>
                                    <li>v20Basic</li>
                                    <li>v20EN16931</li>
                                    <li>v20Extended</li>
                                    <li>v21Minimum</li>
                                    <li>v21BasicWL</li>
                                    <li>v21Basic</li>
                                    <li>v21EN16931</li>
                                    <li>v21Extended</li>
                                    <li>v21XRechnung</li>
                                    <li>v22Minimum</li>
                                    <li>v22BasicWL</li>
                                    <li>v22Basic</li>
                                    <li>v22EN16931</li>
                                    <li>v22Extended</li>
                                    <li>v22XRechnung</li>
                                    <li>v23Minimum</li>
                                    <li>v23BasicWL</li>
                                    <li>v23Basic</li>
                                    <li>v23EN16931</li>
                                    <li>v23Extended</li>
                                    <li>v23XRechnung</li>
                                    <li>v24Minimum</li>
                                    <li>v24BasicWL</li>
                                    <li>v24Basic</li>
                                    <li>v24EN16931</li>
                                    <li>v24Extended</li>
                                    <li>v24XRechnung</li>
                                    <li>v25Minimum</li>
                                    <li>v25BasicWL</li>
                                    <li>v25Basic</li>
                                    <li>v25EN16931</li>
                                    <li>v25Extended</li>
                                    <li>v25XRechnung</li>
                                </ul>
                            </p>
                        </xs:documentation>
                    </xs:annotation>
                </xs:attribute>
            </xs:extension>
        </xs:simpleContent>
    </xs:complexType>
    <xs:complexType name="PdfaErrorCorrectionType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>This parameter can be used to optionally activate automatic error correction.
                    If a PDF/A conversion does not work, this may be due to defective PDF syntax structures in the source document. If error correction is enabled then an attempt will be made to correct these syntax errors automatically.

                </p>
                <p>
                    <b>Important:</b>
                    If the conversion of an existing PDF document to a certain level (e.g. PDF/A-1) does not work, then there must not always be syntax errors in the document. It may also be that the source document does not have all the necessary content (e.g. missing font embedding) that is mandatory for conversion to a certain level. In this case it may be sufficient to switch to a different PDF/A level.
                    Therefore, the conversion report should always be checked first to see if there is really a defective source document before activating error correction.

                    Error correction tries to correct syntax errors such as defective XREF tables or defective objects (defective data streams) in the PDF structure. First the PDF/conversion is performed normally. If errors are then detected so that a valid PDF/A is not created, an attempt is made to perform error correction.
                    If the error correction works, a second pass of the PDF/A conversion is performed. If this run works, then the corresponding PDF/A document is delivered. If not, the corresponding error code and possibly the error report will be delivered.

                </p>
                <p>
                    <b>Important:</b>
                    If error correction is active, then visual and/or content deviations may occur in the converted PDF/A document. If you activate this option, then the resulting document should be checked in any case.

                    It is recommended to perform the PDF/A conversion first without activating the error correction to be sure that the document is not visually and contentwise changed after the conversion. Only if the conversion was not possible (and the error report was checked) should the option be activated in a second call. The PDF/A document of the second call should be checked for visual and content problems.
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:attribute name="enabled" default="false" type="xs:boolean">
            <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>
                    <p>Enables or disables error correction. If the option is set to "true" then PDF syntax errors in the PDF document will be corrected during PDF/A conversion.</p>
                </xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
        </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
    <xs:complexType name="InvoiceRuleValidationType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>Optionally validates a ZUGFeRD/Factur-X/XRechnung invoice XML against an official
                    e-invoicing rule package (KoSIT XRechnung 3.0.2 or Landrix ZUGFeRD 2.5). Two
                    elements use this type, and the same parameters trigger the same check in both:
                    "convert &gt; zugferd &gt; invoiceRuleValidation" checks the invoice supplied with
                    the request, before it is embedded, and "analyze &gt; invoiceRuleValidation" checks
                    an invoice that is already embedded in the uploaded PDF/A document. In "analyze" the
                    invoice is located in the document itself: an attachment named by the XMP
                    "DocumentFileName" pointer, or carrying one of the canonical invoice file names, or
                    marked as an associated file. A document that carries no such attachment, more than
                    one equally qualified one, or one that cannot be read is reported as
                    "state=notEvaluable" with the corresponding reason. An invoice XML without a PDF
                    carrier is checked by the "invoice" operation, which shares all parameters of this
                    type except "mode" (see "InvoiceType").
                </p>
                <p>This is independent of and in addition to webPDF's own XSD validation of the ZUGFeRD
                    schema variant (error code -410), which always runs first in the "convert" branch
                    and is unaffected by this element: a document can be valid against webPDF's own
                    schema and still be rejected here, because the official rule packages check
                    business rules the schema alone cannot express - and vice versa, a document that
                    fails the rule package's own, stricter schema step is reported through the error
                    code documented below (PDFA_ZUGFERD_RULE_VALIDATION_ERROR), never through -410
                    itself.
                </p>
                <p>The two branches differ in how "mode=enforce" surfaces a rejection, because they
                    differ in what the operation returns. In "convert", a rejection aborts the operation
                    with the error code documented on the "zugferd" web service response
                    (PDFA_ZUGFERD_RULE_VALIDATION_ERROR) instead of embedding the invoice; that single
                    error code does NOT by itself distinguish a genuine rule violation from a document
                    that could not be evaluated at all, a distinction available only in the invoice
                    validation report (see "report/invoice.xsd", attributes "state" and "reason") and in
                    a single WARN log entry per request. In "analyze", the operation always returns its
                    analysis report and never a dedicated error code for this check; the rejection
                    decision is instead recorded as "enforcement" on that report's "invoice" element
                    (see "report/pdfa.xsd").
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:attribute name="mode" type="tns:InvoiceValidationModeType" default="disabled">
            <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>
                    <p>"disabled" (default): no rule package is loaded and behaviour is byte-identical to
                        a request without this element at all.
                    </p>
                    <p>"report": the invoice is checked against a rule package and the outcome is added to
                        the "invoice" element of the PDF/A report, but the outcome NEVER changes the
                        result of the operation - in "convert" a rule-violating invoice is still
                        embedded, in "analyze" the document is still analysed and its report still
                        delivered. In "convert" the result is only VISIBLE when a report was additionally
                        requested via "errorReport" and/or "successReport" (both default to "none"); in
                        "analyze" the report IS always the response, so the result is always visible
                        there.
                    </p>
                    <p>"enforce": a document whose rule package assessment is "reject" is, in "convert",
                        rejected with error code -416 instead of being embedded. In "analyze" there is no
                        dedicated error code and the operation still returns its report; the rejection is
                        instead recorded as "enforcement=rejected" on that report's "invoice" element.
                        Whether a document that could not be evaluated at all is also rejected is
                        governed separately by "notEvaluable".
                    </p>
                </xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
        </xs:attribute>
        <xs:attributeGroup ref="tns:InvoiceRuleValidationGroup"/>
    </xs:complexType>
    <xs:complexType name="InvoiceType">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>Validates an electronic invoice XML (ZUGFeRD, Factur-X, XRechnung) that is supplied
                    WITHOUT a PDF carrier: the source document of the request is the invoice XML itself.
                    The check is the same check "analyze &gt; invoiceRuleValidation" runs on an invoice
                    embedded in a PDF/A document - the same rule packages, the same parameters with the
                    same meaning and the same result - only without the PDF/A validation and without the
                    search for the embedded invoice.
                </p>
                <p>The response document is always the invoice validation report, with the standalone
                    root element "report" of "report/invoice.xsd" - also for an invoice that violates the
                    rules and for one that could not be evaluated at all. Exactly as in "analyze", the
                    operation never answers with a dedicated error code for the outcome of the check:
                    the verdict is carried by the report's "state", and a "mode=enforce" decision by its
                    "enforcement" attribute. A source document that is not well-formed XML is reported as
                    "state=notEvaluable" with "reason=sourceDocumentUnreadable", one that exceeds the
                    configured size limit with "reason=documentTooLarge".
                </p>
                <p>The operation needs neither a PDF nor the PDF/A converter at request time, but it is
                    part of the "Pdfa" web service: it is available exactly when that web service is
                    available and licensed.
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:attribute name="mode" type="tns:InvoiceModeType" default="report">
            <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>
                    <p>"report" (default): the invoice is checked against a rule package and the outcome is
                        returned as the invoice validation report.
                    </p>
                    <p>"enforce": the same check, and additionally the enforcement decision is recorded as
                        "enforcement=passed" or "enforcement=rejected" on the report - exactly as in
                        "analyze &gt; invoiceRuleValidation". Whether a document that could not be evaluated
                        at all counts as rejected is governed by "notEvaluable". The operation itself
                        still answers with the report and without an error code.
                    </p>
                    <p>Unlike "invoiceRuleValidation", this attribute knows no "disabled": the presence of
                        the "invoice" element IS the request to check the invoice.
                    </p>
                </xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
        </xs:attribute>
        <xs:attributeGroup ref="tns:InvoiceRuleValidationGroup"/>
    </xs:complexType>
    <xs:attributeGroup name="InvoiceRuleValidationGroup">
        <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
                <p>The parameters of the invoice rule validation that "invoiceRuleValidation" (in
                    "convert &gt; zugferd" and in "analyze") and the "invoice" operation share, with the
                    same meaning in all three places. A parameter that applies to the invoice rule
                    validation as such - for example a later choice of the executing rule engine - belongs
                    here, so that it is available in all three places at once.
                </p>
            </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:attribute name="notEvaluable" type="tns:InvoiceNotEvaluableType" default="reject">
            <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>
                    <p>Only effective under "mode=enforce". Governs the enforcement decision for a
                        document that could NOT be evaluated at all - no rule package matched, a size or
                        depth limit was exceeded, the time budget was exceeded, the configured rule
                        package could not be loaded, (in "analyze") no invoice attachment could be
                        identified or read at all, or (in "invoice") the source document is not
                        well-formed XML. "reject" (default, fail-closed): such a document is treated the
                        same as a genuine rule violation - rejected with error code -416 in "convert", or
                        reported as "enforcement=rejected" in "analyze" and "invoice". "accept": such a
                        document is embedded ("convert") or reported as "enforcement=passed" ("analyze",
                        "invoice") instead. Either way, this attribute NEVER rescues a document that WAS evaluated
                        and rejected by the rule package itself - it only covers the "could not be
                        evaluated" case.
                    </p>
                </xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
        </xs:attribute>
        <xs:attribute name="ruleSet" type="xs:string" use="optional">
            <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>
                    <p>Forces a specific configured rule package identifier (for example "xrechnung" or
                        "zugferd") instead of the automatic, ordered selection. Selects a PACKAGE, not a
                        scenario within it: if the forced package has no scenario matching the document,
                        the outcome is "notEvaluable" - it does NOT fall back to another package.
                    </p>
                    <p>Both built-in packages can declare a matching scenario for the SAME EN 16931-based
                        document (guideline identifier "urn:cen.eu:en16931:2017"); without this override,
                        the server-configured selection order decides which one is used (see
                        "invoiceValidation" in the application configuration schema). Use this attribute when
                        the caller, not the server's default order, must decide which of the two packages
                        such a document is checked against.
                    </p>
                </xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
        </xs:attribute>
        <xs:attribute name="originalReport" type="tns:InvoiceOriginalReportType" default="none">
            <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>
                    <p>Whether the rule package's OWN report - the "Validation Artefact Result List" the
                        package produces while checking the document, and which webPDF otherwise
                        discards - is delivered alongside webPDF's own invoice validation result, and in
                        which form. "none" (default): it is not delivered, and the answer is exactly the
                        answer of a request that does not name this attribute at all. "embedded": it is
                        delivered base64-encoded in the "originalReport" element of the invoice
                        validation result (see "report/invoice.xsd") - complete and unaltered, including
                        its own XML declaration, so that a recipient can hand it to another tool as the
                        standalone document the rule package produced. webPDF neither rewrites nor
                        abridges it, and it is delivered IN ADDITION to webPDF's own result, never
                        instead of it.
                    </p>
                    <p>The payload travels wherever the invoice validation result itself travels, and
                        only there - it is part of the report, not a second response. Under
                        "invoiceRuleValidation/@mode=disabled" no rule package is loaded at all, so there
                        is neither a result nor a payload. In "analyze" and in "invoice" the report IS
                        the response, so an evaluated document carries the payload unless one of the
                        reasons named below removes it. In
                        "convert" a report is delivered only when one was
                        requested - through "successReport" for a document that was embedded, or through
                        "errorReport" for a document rejected under "mode=enforce" - so with both of
                        those at "none" the payload has nowhere to travel and is simply not produced.
                        That is a documented interaction and not an error: asking for the payload never
                        turns a request into a failure, and never makes the operation deliver a report
                        that was not asked for.
                    </p>
                    <p>The ABSENCE of the payload therefore carries no verdict information of its own -
                        "state", "assessment", "reason" and the finding counters are unaffected by it.
                        Every reason it can be absent is described at the element itself in
                        "report/invoice.xsd". The one worth naming here: it is absent whenever no rule
                        package evaluation produced a report at all, which is every
                        "state=notEvaluable" outcome whatever its reason - including the ordinary
                        "analyze" case of a document that carries no invoice attachment. Under
                        "mode=enforce" with "notEvaluable=reject" such a document is still rejected; the
                        rejection and the absent payload are independent statements.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <b>Size:</b>
                        the rule package's own report is a multiple of webPDF's own result, it grows
                        with the number of findings the checked document produces, and the base64
                        encoding adds to that again - a response can grow by orders of magnitude. In
                        "convert", use "errorReport=file" for large reports, which delivers the report as
                        a response document, rather than "errorReport=message"; in "analyze" and in
                        "invoice" the report is always the response document. A server administrator can
                        additionally cap the payload (see "invoiceValidation" in the application
                        configuration schema); above that ceiling the payload is omitted while the
                        verdict and the operation's result stay exactly as they are.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <b>Important, when combined with "errorReport=message" (only in "convert"):</b>
                        the rule package's report carries invoice CONTENT - among other things the
                        supplier, the invoice number, the invoice date and a table of element values
                        taken from the checked document. With "errorReport=message" that content is
                        delivered in the ERROR channel (the REST error body, the SOAP fault) instead of
                        as a report document, and error channels are routinely logged and forwarded by
                        callers, middleware and monitoring. The combination is served rather than
                        refused, but choose it deliberately: "errorReport=file" delivers the same
                        report, with the same payload, as a response document instead.
                    </p>
                </xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
        </xs:attribute>
        <xs:attribute name="originalReportHtml" type="xs:boolean" default="false">
            <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>
                    <p>Whether the human-readable HTML view the rule package embeds in its OWN report is
                        ADDITIONALLY delivered as a payload of its own, in the "originalReportHtml"
                        element of the invoice validation result (see "report/invoice.xsd") - the same
                        element name as this attribute, deliberately. "false" (default): the view is not
                        delivered separately, and the answer is exactly the answer of a request that does
                        not name this attribute at all.
                    </p>
                    <p>Only effective when "originalReport" is not "none": this attribute decides only
                        WHETHER the view travels, never in which form - its delivery form always follows
                        "originalReport". With "originalReport=none" there is no rule package report to
                        take a view out of, so "originalReportHtml" has no effect and asking for it is not
                        an error, exactly like every other documented interaction of this element.
                    </p>
                    <p>The view is EXTRACTED from the rule package's own report, never re-rendered: it is
                        the very HTML fragment that report already embeds. It is delivered UTF-8 encoded
                        and, being a fragment of an XML document rather than a standalone HTML file,
                        carries no character-set declaration of its own - a recipient that serves or
                        stores it as HTML has to state UTF-8 itself. Its absence carries no verdict
                        information of its own; every reason it can be absent is described at the element
                        itself in "report/invoice.xsd". None of them changes "state", "assessment",
                        "reason" or the finding counters, and asking for the view never turns a request
                        into a failure.
                    </p>
                    <p>Subject to the same operator size ceiling as "originalReport" (see
                        "invoiceValidation" in the application configuration schema), measured against the
                        view's own raw, not-yet-encoded size and applied independently of it: a ceiling
                        that suppresses the (larger) report does not by itself suppress the (smaller)
                        view.
                    </p>
                </xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
        </xs:attribute>
    </xs:attributeGroup>
    <xs:simpleType name="InvoiceOriginalReportType">
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="none"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="embedded"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
    <xs:simpleType name="InvoiceValidationModeType">
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="disabled"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="report"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="enforce"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
    <xs:simpleType name="InvoiceModeType">
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="report"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="enforce"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
    <xs:simpleType name="InvoiceNotEvaluableType">
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="reject"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="accept"/>
        </xs:restriction>
    </xs:simpleType>
</xs:schema>